unmanned aircraft system with inoperative equipment or equipment that 
has failed its initial performance checks unless all the following 
requirements are met:
    (1) The inoperative equipment is not--
    (i) Indicated as necessary by the manufacturer of the unmanned 
aircraft pursuant to the manufacturer's operating instructions;
    (ii) Required by subpart H of this part; or
    (iii) Required for specific operations under this part.
    (2) The inoperative equipment is removed from the unmanned 
aircraft, deactivated, or otherwise determined not to interfere with 
the safe operation of the unmanned aircraft.
    (3) A determination is made by a person who is authorized by the 
operator to perform maintenance on the unmanned aircraft that the 
inoperative equipment does not constitute a hazard to the unmanned 
aircraft.
    (4) Information identifying the inoperable equipment is made 
available to the appropriate operations personnel.
","sha256":"80ff8dd76332bfb912ed3a68c7a9e3578f8b804adcee59222b2a7b17586eab8a","document":{"url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-08-07/html/2025-14992.htm","sha256":"2ebbbb6d3ecfe4757a192c1850d67373e75c18d7df52136a607737ee9672f7f7","readPath":"/v1/rule-sources/govinfo.fr.2025-14992/content","sourceId":"govinfo.fr.2025-14992","byteLength":1386012,"contentType":"text/html; charset=utf-8"},"encoding":"utf-8","textSpan":{"end":1292805,"unit":"utf8_byte","start":1291780,"sourceId":"govinfo.fr.2025-14992"},"reference":"Proposed 14 CFR 108.555(a)","byteLength":1025},"target":{"subjectKind":"flight"},"adopted":false,"related":[{"from":{"read":"plan","field":"secondarySubject"},"name":"aircraft","fanOut":false,"requeue":{"windowEnd":{"read":"plan","field":"values.record.windowEndsAt"},"endedWithinDays":7},"whenNone":"empty","subjectKind":"aircraft"}],"section":"108.555","version":1,"wording":{"pass":"The detect-and-avoid equipment recorded on the planned aircraft before the flight is inoperative, and its record names who determined it does not constitute a hazard to the aircraft, and when. Whether that person is one the operator authorizes to perform maintenance, whether the equipment is needed for the operation, and whether the people operating the flight were told, are for a person to review.","attention":"The detect-and-avoid equipment recorded on the planned aircraft before the flight is inoperative, and its record does not name who determined that it does not constitute a hazard to the aircraft, or when.","not_applicable":"No detect-and-avoid equipment is recorded as inoperative on the planned aircraft before the flight. Other inoperative equipment is not in these records; it is for a person to review."},"coverage":"automated","paragraph":"§ 108.555(a)","population":{"of":"in_adoption_dates"},"applicability":[],"adoptionParameters":[]},{"id":"ledger.nprm.108.560.a","title":"Safety management system","digest":"8139de40477f987ebc252584aedd85b26087d07777b38ee2909882774cc51c3b","review":"ai_drafted","source":{"kind":"proposed_regulation","text":"    (a) General. Operators authorized to conduct operations as a 
certificated operator under this subpart must develop, implement, and 
keep current a safety management system that meets the requirements of 
